Q1.
Is problem me tumhe ek graph diya gaya hai jisme n vertices hain aur har edge ka ek weight hai. Tumhe ek aisa path find karna 
hai jo har vertex ko exactly ek baar visit kare (isko Hamiltonian walk bolte hain) aur is path ka total cost minimum ho. Simple 
language me: “saare nodes ek baar cover karo aur cost sabse kam rakho.



Mask ka concept:---
Mask ek binary number hota hai jo batata hai kaunse vertices visit ho chuke hain. Agar n = 4 hai aur mask = 1011 hai, 
iska matlab nodes {0,1,3} visit ho chuke hain.
Bitmask ka use isliye karte 
hain kyunki ye subsets ko efficiently represent karta hai aur DP me use karna easy ho jata hai.


DP state ka meaning:---
dp[mask][i] ka matlab hai: “mask me jo nodes hain wo sab visit ho chuke hain aur path currently node i pe end ho raha hai, aur is situation ka 
minimum cost kya hai”. Yeh bahut important definition hai kyunki poora solution isi pe depend karta hai.


Base case:---
Jab mask me sirf ek hi node hai (maan lo node i), tab cost 0 hoga. Kyunki tumne sirf ek 
node visit kiya hai, koi edge traverse nahi ki. Isliye dp[1<<i][i] = 0 hota hai.



Transition (core idea):---
Agar tum i pe end kar rahe ho aur mask given hai, iska matlab tum i se pehle kisi node j pe the. To hum check karte hain:
dp[mask][i] = min(dp[mask without i][j] + cost(j,i))
Yahan “mask without i” ka matlab hai ki hum i ko hata ke previous state dekh rahe hain. 
Aur phir j → i edge ka cost add kar rahe hain. 
Ye hi DP ka core logic hai.




Intuition (sabse important):---
DP ko samajhne ka best tareeka hai ye sochna ki “last node kaun hai”. Hum path ko forward nahi bana rahe, 
balki reverse soch rahe hain: agar last node i hai, to usse pehle kaun tha? 
Ye thinking DP ko bahut simple bana deti hai.


Final answer kaise milta hai:---
Jab sab nodes visit ho chuke honge (full mask = (1<<n)-1), tab path kisi bhi node pe end ho sakta hai. Isliye hum sab i ke liye check karte hain:
answer = min(dp[full_mask][i])
Jo minimum hoga wahi final answer hai.



Path reconstruction ka idea:---
DP me hum cost store karte hain, lekin path bhi nikalna hai. Iske liye hum parent[mask][i] store karte hain jo batata hai ki i pe aane se pehle kaun sa node j tha. 
Fir hum last node se start karke reverse me jaate hain aur mask se nodes remove karte jaate hain.
End me path ko reverse kar dete hain.




Complexity:---
Is DP me total states 2^n * n hote hain aur har state me n transitions try karte hain. 
Isliye total time complexity O(n^2 * 2^n) hoti hai. 
Space complexity O(n * 2^n) hoti hai.





